{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/810396-lfm-skype-game-of-1920-s-lovecraft-influenced-vtm","id":810396,"title":"LFM: Skype Game of 1920's Lovecraft-influenced VtM.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-16T16:34:35-08:00","id":810396,"title":"LFM: Skype Game of 1920's Lovecraft-influenced VtM.","content":"I'd like to recruit 1-2 more players for my online Voice-over-Skype VtM game. It runs Saturday nights at 7PM Eastern Time, generally for 4 hours. We use Roll20 to handle dice and variable traits, plus minor illustrations.<br /> <br /> The game is set in Arkham, MA in the late 1920s and strongly influenced by Lovecraftian themes. Here's the game blurb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Arkham by Night<br /> <br /> The city of Arkham is famous for its university, the wealth of its industrialists, and the families that have been part of its society since the founding of the nation. It's feared for the darkness that creeps through its streets after nightfall, and the shadows that surge up from the riverbanks and out of the bay after the sun sets. Arkham is full of glitz, glamour, gore and gin. <br /> <br /> You've all been touched by those shadows. You've all seen something lurking at the threshold, darting away from the sunlight. Maybe you saw something that the police explained away. Maybe you lost someone and had it hushed up. It was suspicious, and frightening at times. Now you aren't suspicious anymore, because the darkness broke into your life and stole you away. Now you're one of them. And you creep through the streets after nightfall.<br /> <br /> But vampires are not the most fearsome things in the night. Especially not since the Miskatonic University's much-publicized expedition to Ninevah. They brought back many artifacts... and maybe more. Because ever since then, the darkness has been darker, and the night more full of terrors. <br /> <br /> Children are going missing, the homeless are vanishing from the streets, and even some of the city's undead have gone without a trace. Something is hunting in Arkham, and the eldest vampire in the city was their latest victim. With her gone, who can feel safe?</i> </div> </div> </div>The only Clans allowed are Brujah, Cappadocian, Gangrel, Toreador and Ventrue. I'm open to variations, like Auspex Ventrue and Greek Gangrel, but beyond that I'm not real flexible. The standard Sect structure is not a key feature of my games (IE: no big focus on Prince, Primogen, Archons, Harpies, etc). You shouldn't expect anything but the playable Clans and default Disciplines to conform to standard VtM. If interested, take a gander at the <a href=\"http://wiki.stryck.com/WoD/ArkhamByNight\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicle Wiki.</a> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you're interested, I can be contacted via email (piratezombie is my gmail) or via skype (my ID is somnorianbadgermonster).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T20:34:00-08:00","id":815209,"title":"","content":"Still looking for 2 more players. I have three already, but we'd like to get to 5 total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link